  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "The strongest completed setting is RNA-only multiprofile scVI_n200 with avgpool/transformer, reaching about 0.65 validation accuracy, while image-only ResNet50 single-profile is weak at 0.21 and no fusion has yet been tested. The key uncertainty is whether adding image features to the best RNA multiprofile representation provides complementary signal or whether the weak image baseline makes multimodal fusion unhelpful. config_030 tests this directly by extending the strong RNA-only multiprofile scVI_n200 avgpool setting with ResNet50 image features and the simplest concat fusion, keeping the RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation fixed. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the strongest known direction, uses a simple comparison to isolate the effect of adding image features and fusion, avoids relying on the very small transformer-aggregation advantage or more complex weighted/ViT choices, and directly informs whether further multimodal exploration is worthwhile under the limited budget."
}

